```

The root cause: `Application.Selector.setMock` was called with the mock only, so the fflib `SelectorFactory` did not resolve it for `Opportunity.SObjectType` — the real `OpportunitiesSelector` ran instead, returned nothing (empty SOQL on fake ids), so no opportunity was ever processed. The fix is the two-argument form: `Application.Selector.setMock(Opportunity.SObjectType, selectorMock)`. Everything else (ordering fake for the gateway, ApexMocks stubbing/verification) stays as designed.

