```

What changed:

- **`Application.Selector.setMock(Opportunity.SObjectType, selectorMock)`** (two-argument form) instead of the single-argument `setMock(selectorMock)`. The single-argument call did not register the mock for the `Opportunity` SObjectType, so `OpportunitiesSelector.newInstance()` in the service resolved to the real selector, ran a SOQL against fake ids, returned nothing, and consequently no opportunity was ever invoiced (hence result 0 and zero `createInvoice` calls in every data-driven test). The two-argument form is the documented fflib pattern and makes the selector mock effective while keeping the test free of SOQL.
- Extracted the repeated wiring into `givenSelectorFor` / `givenUnitOfWork` helpers (used consistently in all tests) to keep the mock injection correct everywhere.
- Added an assertion in the authentication-failure test that `authenticate()` was attempted (guards against the exception path being skipped entirely).

