```apex
public with sharing class CaseSurveyDispatcher {

    private static final Integer MAX_ENQUEUE_PER_TXN = 50;

    public static void dispatch(List<Case> newList, Map<Id, Case> oldMap) {
        List<Id> caseIds = new List<Id>();
        for (Case newCase : newList) {
            Case oldCase = oldMap.get(newCase.Id);
            Boolean wasClosed = (oldCase != null && oldCase.IsClosed);
            if (newCase.IsClosed && !wasClosed && newCase.ContactId != null) {
                caseIds.add(newCase.Id);
            }
        }

        if (caseIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Enqueue at most 50 jobs per transaction (the platform limit).
        // Any overflow is handed to the last job, which chains itself so
        // every case still runs in its own job execution.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < caseIds.size(); i++) {
            if (i < MAX_ENQUEUE_PER_TXN - 1) {
                System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(caseIds[i]));
            } else {
                List<Id> tail = caseIds.subList(i + 1, caseIds.size());
                System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(caseIds[i], tail));
                break;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### What changed and why

1. **Fix for `Too many queueable jobs added to the queue: 51`** — `System.enqueueJob` is limited to 50 calls per transaction. The nightly cleanup closes up to 200 cases in one API call, so one-enqueue-per-case alone breaks the limit. The dispatcher now enqueues at most 50 jobs; any remaining case Ids are passed into the last enqueued job, which chains itself (a queueable may enqueue exactly one child job from `execute()`), so **every case is still processed in its own job execution**, just via chaining for cases 51–200.

2. **Failure isolation preserved** — each case's task creation is wrapped in `try/catch` inside the job, so one failing case is logged and skipped without preventing the chain (or sibling jobs) from handling the remaining cases.

3. **Everything else unchanged** — the not-closed → closed transition check, the contact filter (skip before enqueueing, and re-check inside the job), the re-query for fresh `CaseNumber`, and the `with sharing` security model all remain as before.

